["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Fresh snow writes down everything that moved last night. For a beginner it is the best teacher there is.</p></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-deer-trail-snow.jpg\" alt=\"Deer tracks on a snowy trail. One line, prints close together: walking.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Deer tracks on a snowy trail. One line, prints close together: walking. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Peter Cooper Jr., CC0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deer_tracks_in_snow_on_trail_at_McKinstry_Brook_WMA_2026-02-01.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Who, how many, which way, how long ago, and what it did.</li><li>Late Region 3 deer season is mostly snow hunting <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this session covers</summary><ul><li>Snow turns every animal into an open book: who, how many, which way, how long ago, and what it did.</li><li>This session: reading a snow track, aging in snow, backtracking versus following, tracking a wounded animal, tracking safely, and when to stop.</li><li>Late season Region 3 deer hunting, November into early December, is mostly snow hunting on <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Winter range\">Winter range</button> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Track basics are in <a href=\"#/s/tracks\">Tracks</a>. Winter feed and cover are in <a href=\"#/s/food-water-cover\">Food, water and cover</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Buck or doe from urine in snow, hunter lore 60 percent. A doe squats, so the yellow stain sits behind the hind prints. A buck dribbles while walking, so the stain sits between or ahead of the hind prints. Travel is up the page.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Urine in snow: doe or buck?</text>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"42\" width=\"185\" height=\"190\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#eef2f6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"205\" y=\"42\" width=\"185\" height=\"190\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#eef2f6\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#6b4f35\">\n    <g transform=\"translate(80 100) scale(.8)\"><path d=\"M-2 -20 C-9 -16 -13 -2 -12 12 C-11 19 -3 20 -2 14 Z\"/><path d=\"M2 -20 C9 -16 13 -2 12 12 C11 19 3 20 2 14 Z\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(125 100) scale(.8)\"><path d=\"M-2 -20 C-9 -16 -13 -2 -12 12 C-11 19 -3 20 -2 14 Z\"/><path d=\"M2 -20 C9 -16 13 -2 12 12 C11 19 3 20 2 14 Z\"/></g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(275 100) scale(.8)\"><path d=\"M-2 -20 C-9 -16 -13 -2 -12 12 C-11 19 -3 20 -2 14 Z\"/><path d=\"M2 -20 C9 -16 13 -2 12 12 C11 19 3 20 2 14 Z\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(320 100) scale(.8)\"><path d=\"M-2 -20 C-9 -16 -13 -2 -12 12 C-11 19 -3 20 -2 14 Z\"/><path d=\"M2 -20 C9 -16 13 -2 12 12 C11 19 3 20 2 14 Z\"/></g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(285 175) scale(.8)\"><path d=\"M-2 -20 C-9 -16 -13 -2 -12 12 C-11 19 -3 20 -2 14 Z\"/><path d=\"M2 -20 C9 -16 13 -2 12 12 C11 19 3 20 2 14 Z\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(320 205) scale(.8)\"><path d=\"M-2 -20 C-9 -16 -13 -2 -12 12 C-11 19 -3 20 -2 14 Z\"/><path d=\"M2 -20 C9 -16 13 -2 12 12 C11 19 3 20 2 14 Z\"/></g>\n  </g>\n  <ellipse cx=\"102\" cy=\"160\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#e0c341\" opacity=\".8\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#e0c341\" opacity=\".85\"><ellipse cx=\"298\" cy=\"65\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\"/><ellipse cx=\"297\" cy=\"100\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\"/><ellipse cx=\"300\" cy=\"140\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\"/><ellipse cx=\"302\" cy=\"160\" rx=\"5\" ry=\"3\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M30 210 V150\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M30 142 l-7 12 h14 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Doe</text>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">squats: stain behind</text>\n  <text x=\"297\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Buck</text>\n  <text x=\"297\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">dribbles: between, ahead</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Find the clearest print in shallow snow (Tip).</li></ul><ul><li>Wide straddle, big prints, drag marks: a buck worth following <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: drag marks, counting and urine lore</summary><ul><li>Snow shows size and shape clearly in the first few centimetres. Deep powder blurs everything into holes; look for the clearest print in a shallow spot (Tip).</li><li>Hoof drag marks run into each print from behind. Bucks and older deer drag more; a long drag in shallow snow suggests a heavy animal (hunter lore) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>A wide straddle, big prints and drag marks together is buck sign worth following. A big doe can fool you <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Deer in snow walk in each other's prints. Count the trails leaving a bed area, not the prints (Tip).</li><li>Stot groups in snow are easy to read: 4 holes close together, a long gap, 4 more <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Urine in snow: a doe squats, so the stain is behind the hind prints. A buck dribbles while walking, so the stain is between or ahead of the hind prints (hunter lore) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-moose-trail-snow.jpg\" alt=\"A moose ploughed through deep snow.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A moose ploughed through deep snow. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: NPS staff, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moose_Browse_Collection,_Yukon-Charley_Rivers,_2003_2_(1482c7be-3b1f-42da-844e-544383bbd5da).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-elk-trail-snow.jpg\" alt=\"Elk walk single file in each other's prints.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Elk walk single file in each other's prints. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Loren Lane ( MORA ), Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elk_tracks_in_snow._111984._slide_(ba1503e681a9402f97f934fbd6d8a5d8).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 340\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Aging a track in snow. Fresh: sharp walls and loose snow crumbs that fall apart when poked. Hours: crumbs bonded into a crust, trackers call it sintering. Sun: edges rounded, floor glazed. Wind or new snow: drifted in or filled. Ice floor and ice walls: made before last night's freeze. Cold clear nights keep tracks crisp for days, so trust the crumbs and your own test print.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"340\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Aging a track in snow</text>\n  <g fill=\"#eef2f6\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\">\n    <path d=\"M10 70 H34 V105 H70 V70 H94 V125 H10 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M108 70 H132 V105 H168 V70 H192 V125 H108 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M206 70 H222 Q234 76 236 98 Q240 105 250 105 Q262 105 264 98 Q266 76 278 70 H294 V125 H206 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M304 70 H322 Q330 84 334 96 Q348 100 362 96 Q366 84 374 70 H392 V125 H304 Z\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"64\" r=\"4\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"62\" r=\"4\"/><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"64\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"62\" r=\"3\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M116 66 q8 -6 16 0 M168 66 q8 -6 16 0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <path d=\"M238 104 Q250 100 262 104\" stroke=\"#9cc3e6\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <path d=\"M322 84 Q348 94 372 84\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"#fff\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"52\" y=\"150\">Fresh</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"150\">Hours</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"150\">Sun</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"150\">Wind, snow</text></g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"52\" y=\"170\">loose crumbs</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"188\">sharp walls</text>\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"170\">crumbs</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"188\">bonded</text>\n    <text x=\"250\" y=\"170\">rounded,</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"188\">glazed</text>\n    <text x=\"348\" y=\"170\">drifted</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"188\">or filled</text>\n  </g>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"208\" width=\"380\" height=\"120\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#eef2f6\"/>\n  <text x=\"24\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\">Tests</text>\n  <text x=\"24\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Poke a crumb: holds together means time passed</text>\n  <text x=\"24\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Ice floor and walls: before last night's freeze</text>\n  <text x=\"24\" y=\"302\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Make your own print each hour: your clock</text>\n  <text x=\"24\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">Cold still nights keep tracks crisp for days</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Loose crumbs: fresh. Bonded crumbs: hours <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Your own test print is your clock (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every snow aging clue</summary><ul><li>Fresh: sharp walls and loose crumbs of snow scattered around the print that have not bonded <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>The crumbs bond into a crust within hours. Trackers call this sintering. Poke a crumb; if it holds together, time has passed <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Sun rounds the edges and glazes the floor. Wind drifts snow into the print. New snow fills it <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Compare the snow in the print with the snow on the ground. 2 cm of fresh snow in a print after a 10 cm fall means it was made early in the storm (Tip).</li><li>Cold clear Interior nights with no wind keep a track crisp for days. In that weather trust the snow crumbs and your own test print, not the edges <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Melt and refreeze: a print with an ice floor and ice walls was made before last night's freeze <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Make your own print beside it every hour. Watch how yours ages; that is your clock (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, bird's eye view. Wind blows from the left. A buck track in snow turns downwind toward thick timber where the deer is likely bedded. Walking the track would carry your scent to the bed. Instead the hunter leaves the track, loops wide, and comes toward the timber from downwind with the wind in their face.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#eef2f6\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><polygon points=\"235,120 247,82 259,120\"/><polygon points=\"265,130 277,92 289,130\"/><polygon points=\"250,160 262,122 274,160\"/><polygon points=\"285,165 297,127 309,165\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"270\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">likely bed</text>\n  <g stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M10 50 H80 m-12 -8 l12 8 l-12 8\"><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;16 0;0 0\" dur=\"2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></path></g>\n  <text x=\"96\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\">Wind</text>\n  <path d=\"M30 270 C 90 250, 120 200, 170 190 S 220 160, 245 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 7\"/>\n  <text x=\"40\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">buck track</text>\n  <path id=\"sg-snow-loop-path\" d=\"M30 270 C 90 250, 120 200, 170 190 C 220 240, 330 270, 380 220 C 395 190, 380 160, 355 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 6\" opacity=\"0\">\n    <animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"0.2s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></path>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"2.2s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <path d=\"M175 185 L240 150\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M195 158 l18 18 M213 158 l-18 18\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n    <text x=\"190\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">scent to the bed</text></g>\n  <g><circle r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text y=\"-14\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text>\n    <animateMotion dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"><mpath href=\"#sg-snow-loop-path\"/></animateMotion></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"7s\" dur=\".5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"70\" width=\"210\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n    <text x=\"125\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Loop: wind in your face</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Track turns downwind? Loop around it. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Backtrack to learn its life. Follow to catch it (Tip).</li><li>Look ahead, not down. Glass every few steps (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: backtrack or follow in detail</summary><ul><li><strong>Backtrack</strong> (walk the trail the way it came) to learn where the deer fed, bedded and crossed. You will not catch the deer, but you will learn its life (Tip).</li><li><strong>Follow</strong> (walk the way it went) to catch up with it. The trail tells you when you are close: feeding turns to walking, then a single line going uphill, then a bed (hunter lore) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Follow with the wind in your face or across you. If the trail turns downwind, loop around rather than walking your scent to the bed (Tip).</li><li>Go slow when the track shows the deer slowed: meandering, nibbling, a dribble of urine, a short stand. It is near its bed <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Look ahead, not down. Every few steps stop and glass the cover ahead and above (Tip). See <a href=\"#/s/glassing\">Glassing</a>.</li><li>Scouting rule: backtrack in the morning after a snowfall, follow in the afternoon toward beds that face the sun (Tip).</li></ul><aside class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Tip (opinion)</div><p>Big woods trackers walk a buck track until he beds, then stalk the bed from above. It takes all day and fails more often than it works. For a beginner, backtracking teaches more.</p></aside></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Blood colour and how long to wait. Bright pink and frothy: lungs, wait about 30 minutes. Dark red: liver or muscle, wait hours. Green or brown smear: gut, wait hours. Pushing a wounded animal makes it run farther.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Read the blood, then wait</text>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"44\" width=\"380\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#eef2f6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"116\" width=\"380\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#eef2f6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"188\" width=\"380\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#eef2f6\"/>\n  <g><circle cx=\"45\" cy=\"76\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#f08080\"/><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"70\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#fff\"/><circle cx=\"52\" cy=\"80\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#fff\"/></g>\n  <circle cx=\"45\" cy=\"148\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#7b1414\"/>\n  <path d=\"M30 220 q15 -10 30 0 q-15 10 -30 0 Z\" fill=\"#6b6b2b\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><text x=\"75\" y=\"72\">Pink, frothy</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"144\">Dark red</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"216\">Green or brown</text></g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><text x=\"75\" y=\"94\">lungs</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"166\">liver or muscle</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"238\">gut</text></g>\n  <g font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"end\"><text x=\"378\" y=\"82\">30 min</text><text x=\"378\" y=\"154\">hours</text><text x=\"378\" y=\"226\">hours</text></g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Push it and it runs farther (70%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Mark where it stood and where you last saw it. Then wait (Tip).</li></ul><ul><li>You must make all reasonable effort to find it <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 470\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"470\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Grid search from the last blood</text>\n\n  <!-- blood trail coming in from the top left -->\n  <path d=\"M30 60 C 70 70, 90 95, 120 110 S 170 130, 200 150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 6\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#e8590c\">\n    <circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"64\" r=\"4\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"72\" cy=\"78\" r=\"4\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"105\" cy=\"100\" r=\"3.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"3\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"172\" cy=\"136\" r=\"2.5\"/>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"26\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Blood trail, flagged</text>\n  <g fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\">\n    <rect x=\"56\" y=\"80\" width=\"6\" height=\"14\"/>\n    <rect x=\"124\" y=\"120\" width=\"6\" height=\"14\"/>\n  </g>\n\n  <!-- last blood -->\n  <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"150\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"214\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">LAST BLOOD</text>\n  <text x=\"214\" y=\"164\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">flag it, return here</text>\n\n  <!-- circles -->\n  <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"150\" r=\"40\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"150\" r=\"80\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/>\n  <text x=\"168\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">1: circle 20 m</text>\n  <text x=\"150\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">2: circle 40 m</text>\n\n  <!-- lanes -->\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">3: lanes, 10 m apart, stay in sight of each other</text>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\">\n    <path d=\"M40 310 H340\"/>\n    <path d=\"M340 310 V335\"/>\n    <path d=\"M340 335 H40\"/>\n    <path d=\"M40 335 V360\"/>\n    <path d=\"M40 360 H340\"/>\n    <path d=\"M340 360 V385\"/>\n    <path d=\"M340 385 H40\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <path d=\"M330 304 L342 310 L330 316 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M50 329 L38 335 L50 341 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M330 354 L342 360 L330 366 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M50 379 L38 385 L50 391 Z\"/>\n  </g>\n  <!-- two searchers -->\n  <g stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\">\n    <circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"300\" r=\"5\"/>\n    <path d=\"M90 305 V318 M82 311 H98 M90 318 L84 328 M90 318 L96 328\" fill=\"none\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"325\" r=\"5\"/>\n    <path d=\"M90 330 V343 M82 336 H98 M90 343 L84 353 M90 343 L96 353\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"104\" y=\"304\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">You</text>\n  <text x=\"104\" y=\"330\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Brother, one lane over</text>\n\n  <!-- downhill / water -->\n  <path d=\"M355 150 L385 210\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <path d=\"M378 196 L387 214 L370 208 Z\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n  <text x=\"392\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"end\">Downhill and water:</text>\n  <text x=\"392\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"end\">check these first</text>\n\n  <!-- legend -->\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"416\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Walk beside the blood line, never on it.</text>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"436\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Lost it? Back to the last flag, then circles, then lanes.</text>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"456\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">Orange: blood and flags. Dashed: search pattern.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: wounded animal details</summary><ul><li>Mark the spot where the animal stood when you shot and the spot where you last saw it, then wait (Tip).</li><li>Wait about 30 minutes for a heart or lung hit; hours for a single lung, liver or gut hit <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>. Pushing a wounded animal makes it run farther <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Blood: bright pink and frothy is lungs. Dark red is liver or muscle. A green or brown smear is gut <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Snow makes blood easy to see and shows the bed, the stumble, and the drag of a leg. Mark every blood spot with flagging you will remove later (Tip).</li><li>Lost the blood? Walk small circles out from the last spot and check every trail leaving it. A wounded deer often heads downhill and toward water or thick cover <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>You must make all reasonable effort to locate, dispatch and retrieve game you kill, cripple or wound <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Synopsis page 12, Retrieval.</li><li>Full after the shot steps: <a href=\"#/s/after-the-shot\">After the shot</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Avalanche terrain. Slopes around 30 degrees and steeper can slide once there is enough snow. Open slopes, gullies and the run out zone below them are all danger. Gentle, treed ground is safer. Take an Avalanche Skills Training level 1 course before you hunt steep snow.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Avalanche terrain</text>\n  <path d=\"M20 250 L230 250 L380 60 L380 250 Z\" fill=\"#eef2f6\"/>\n  <path d=\"M230 250 L380 60\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n  <path d=\"M120 250 L230 250\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"10\" opacity=\".5\"/>\n  <path d=\"M265 250 A 35 35 0 0 0 258 228\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <text x=\"275\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">30 degrees +</text>\n  <path d=\"M320 120 L300 160 M340 110 L310 190\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/>\n  <text x=\"270\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"end\">can slide</text>\n  <text x=\"170\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">run out</text>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><polygon points=\"30,250 40,220 50,250\"/><polygon points=\"60,250 70,215 80,250\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"55\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">gentle, treed</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Avalanche Skills Training 1: 2 days, before steep snow</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Set a turn around time and keep it (Tip).</li><li>Leave a <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Trip plan\">Trip plan</button>. Carry a <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Satellite messenger\">Satellite messenger</button> (Tip).</li></ul><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Region 3: no motor vehicles except snowmobiles above 1,700 m off roads and trails <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Never shoot from a vehicle <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</p></aside><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: safety details and the snowmobile rules</summary><ul><li>Snow tracking pulls you far from the truck. Set a turn around time before you start and keep it (Tip).</li><li>Leave a <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Trip plan\">Trip plan</button> with someone at home. Carry a <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Satellite messenger\">Satellite messenger</button> in the Thompson backcountry (Tip). See <a href=\"#/s/bush-safety\">Bush safety</a>.</li><li>Avalanche terrain starts around 30 degrees of slope once there is enough snow to slide. Open slopes, gullies and the run outs below them can slide in November <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>. Avalanche Canada forecasts cover the North Columbia and South Columbia regions near Kamloops <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>An AST (Avalanche Skills Training) level 1 course is 2 days. Take it before you hunt steep snow country (Tip).</li><li>Cold: wet feet and a sweaty back at dusk are the start of hypothermia. Layer, stop to vent, carry a dry base layer (Tip). See <a href=\"#/s/what-to-wear\">What to wear</a>.</li><li>River and lake ice in November is not trustworthy. Do not cross to save a kilometre (Tip).</li><li>Driving: FSRs (Forest Service Roads) in snow need chains, a shovel and a tow strap. Tell your brother which road (Tip).</li></ul><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Region 3: motor vehicles except snowmobiles are prohibited above 1,700 m except on existing roads and trails <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Snowmobiles may not be used for hunting year round in <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"MU\">MU</button> (Management Unit) areas 3-45 and 3-46, and from 1 April to 14 December in MU 3-28 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Shooting wildlife from a motor vehicle is unlawful anywhere <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</p></aside></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 520\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Flowchart: keep tracking or stop? Question 1: is there legal light left? If no, mark the track, go home, come back at first light. Question 2: is the ground safe, with no avalanche slope, cliff, ice or private land without consent? If no, stop. Question 3: fresh grizzly or cougar tracks on top of yours? If yes, back out. Question 4: tired, wet or unsure of the way out? If yes, stop. Question 5: an unwounded deer walking straight with the day half gone? If yes, stop. If you pass every question, keep going slowly. A wounded animal: keep going while there is light and safe ground, and return at first light if you lose it.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"520\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Keep tracking or stop?</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"44\" width=\"220\" height=\"54\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"120\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1. Legal light left?</text>\n<path d=\"M230 71 H262\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"246\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No</text>\n<rect x=\"262\" y=\"48\" width=\"130\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f6dccb\"/>\n<text x=\"327\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mark it.</text>\n<text x=\"327\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Back at first light</text>\n<path d=\"M120 98 V114\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"114\" width=\"220\" height=\"54\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"120\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2. Safe ground? No avalanche,</text>\n<text x=\"120\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">cliff, ice or private land</text>\n<path d=\"M230 141 H262\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"246\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No</text>\n<rect x=\"262\" y=\"118\" width=\"130\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f6dccb\"/>\n<text x=\"327\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stop.</text>\n<text x=\"327\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Do not follow</text>\n<path d=\"M120 168 V184\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"184\" width=\"220\" height=\"54\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"120\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3. Fresh grizzly or cougar</text>\n<text x=\"120\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">tracks on top of yours?</text>\n<path d=\"M230 211 H262\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"246\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Yes</text>\n<rect x=\"262\" y=\"188\" width=\"130\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f6dccb\"/>\n<text x=\"327\" y=\"216\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Back out now</text>\n<path d=\"M120 238 V254\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"254\" width=\"220\" height=\"54\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"120\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4. Tired, wet, unsure of</text>\n<text x=\"120\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">the way out?</text>\n<path d=\"M230 281 H262\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"246\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Yes</text>\n<rect x=\"262\" y=\"258\" width=\"130\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f6dccb\"/>\n<text x=\"327\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stop.</text>\n<text x=\"327\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Head out</text>\n<path d=\"M120 308 V324\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"324\" width=\"220\" height=\"54\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"120\" y=\"346\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5. Unwounded, walking straight,</text>\n<text x=\"120\" y=\"366\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">day half gone?</text>\n<path d=\"M230 351 H262\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"246\" y=\"344\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Yes</text>\n<rect x=\"262\" y=\"328\" width=\"130\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f6dccb\"/>\n<text x=\"327\" y=\"346\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stop.</text>\n<text x=\"327\" y=\"364\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You will not catch it</text>\n<path d=\"M120 378 V398\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"398\" width=\"220\" height=\"44\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"426\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Keep going, slowly</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"456\" width=\"380\" height=\"58\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"480\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wounded animal: keep going while light</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"500\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">and ground allow. Back at first light.</text>\n</svg></figure><ul><li>A buck is not worth a night out (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: when to stop, in words</summary><ul><li>Stop when legal light ends: one hour after sunset for game other than migratory birds <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Mark the track and come back at first light (Tip).</li><li>Stop when the track crosses into terrain you cannot handle: avalanche slopes, cliffs, ice, or private land without consent (Tip).</li><li>Stop when the animal is walking steadily in a straight line and the day is half gone. It is not bedding; you will not catch it <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Stop when you are tired, wet or unsure of the way out. A buck is not worth a night out (Tip).</li><li>Stop and back out if you find fresh grizzly or cougar tracks on top of your own (Tip).</li><li>A wounded animal changes the rule: keep going while there is light and safe ground, and return at first light if you lose it (95% on the duty to retrieve, Tip on the method).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-deer-trail-snow.jpg\" alt=\"Count trails on south and west slopes.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Count trails on south and west slopes. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Peter Cooper Jr., CC0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deer_tracks_in_snow_on_trail_at_McKinstry_Brook_WMA_2026-02-01.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-grouse-snow-roost.jpg\" alt=\"Grouse roost holes: small game country.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Grouse roost holes: small game country. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Cephas, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bonasa_umbellus_snow_hole.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/snowshoe-hare-winter.jpg\" alt=\"Snowshoe hare: small game for a rifle or shotgun day.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Snowshoe hare: small game for a rifle or shotgun day. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: D. Gordon E. Robertson, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Snowshoe_Hare,_Shirleys_Bay.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><ul><li>December to February teaches you deer numbers (Tip).</li><li>Keep your distance: deep snow costs deer fat (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: winter scouting details</summary><ul><li>December to February on winter range teaches you more about deer numbers than any October walk (Tip).</li><li>Count trails, beds and browse lines on south and west slopes below about 760 m north of Kamloops <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Note where tracks cross roads; those are year round crossings (Tip).</li><li>Bucks drop antlers from late December into March. Shed hunting in spring shows you where bucks wintered <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Keep your distance in winter. Pushing deer in deep snow costs them fat they cannot replace (Tip).</li><li>Snowshoe hare and grouse tracks tell you where small game lives for a .22 LR (Long Rifle) or shotgun day (Tip). Check seasons in the <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Synopsis\">Synopsis</button> <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Snow tells the truth. Walk the track backward to learn, forward to hunt, and home before dark either way.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Reading a 3 day old track as fresh on a cold shaded slope.</li><li>Following a wounded deer 10 minutes after the shot. It runs a kilometre and you lose it.</li><li>Chasing a track onto steep open snow with no avalanche training or gear.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>After the first snow, pick a deer trail and backtrack it for 1 hour. Find where it fed, where it crossed a road or creek, and where it bedded. Draw the route on your map and in the Journal.</p></aside></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-md-doe-sage-snow.jpg\" alt=\"Snow tells the truth.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Snow tells the truth. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain-Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mule_Deer_Doe_in_Southwest_Wyoming_(23267627529).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Snow tells the truth. Walk the track backward to learn, forward to hunt, and home before dark either way.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Reading a 3 day old track as fresh on a cold shaded slope.</li><li>Following a wounded deer 10 minutes after the shot. It runs a kilometre and you lose it.</li><li>Chasing a track onto steep open snow with no avalanche training or gear.</li></ul></aside>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-elk-trail-snow.jpg\" alt=\"Backtrack one trail for 1 hour after the first snow.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Backtrack one trail for 1 hour after the first snow. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Loren Lane ( MORA ), Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elk_tracks_in_snow._111984._slide_(ba1503e681a9402f97f934fbd6d8a5d8).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>After the first snow, backtrack one deer trail for 1 hour. Find where it fed, crossed and bedded. Draw the route in the Journal.</p></aside>","<ul><li>BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028, <a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/sports-recreation-arts-and-culture/outdoor-recreation/fishing-and-hunting/hunting/regulations/hunting-trapping-synopsis.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">full synopsis</a>, read directly from the downloaded synopsis text: page 11 item 22 (shooting from a vehicle), page 11, item 38 (hours) and the Retrieval rule, Region 3 page 33 (motor vehicles above 1,700 m, snowmobile closures). Checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul>","<ul><li>Search previews (direct reading blocked in this environment), checked 2026-10-01:<ul><li><a href=\"https://www.adfg.alaska.gov/index.cfm?adfg=wildlifenews.view_article&amp;articles_id=636\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Alaska Department of Fish and Game, winter tracking</a> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>: aging, sintering, cold Interior tracks.</li><li><a href=\"https://nature-mentor.com/how-to-tell-if-animal-tracks-are-fresh/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nature Mentor, how to tell if tracks are fresh</a> and <a href=\"https://www.thefairchase.com/fieldnotes/how-to-track-deer-in-the-snow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Fair Chase, how to track deer in the snow</a> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.themeateater.com/hunt/big-game/how-to-blood-trail-and-track-game-animals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MeatEater, how to blood trail</a> and <a href=\"https://bowhuntersunited.com/2023/12/12/making-sense-of-blood-trails-a-guide-for-whitetail-recovery/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bowhunters United, making sense of blood trails</a> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>: wait times, blood colour.</li><li><a href=\"https://avalanche.ca/training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Avalanche Canada, training</a> and <a href=\"https://avalog.co/regions/north-columbia\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Avalog, North Columbia forecasts</a> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>: AST 1, forecast regions.</li></ul></li></ul><ul><li>Willms 1976, <a href=\"https://cdnsciencepub.com/doi/pdf/10.4141/cjas76-065\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">deer winter range near Kamloops</a>, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Buck track and urine lore: big woods tracking tradition, labelled Tip or 60%.</li></ul>"]